## 2. Task Tables

| Name | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|------|------|----------|----------|------------------|---------------|
| **AT1: Query Patient Record** | Query the hospital database for patient ability to fetch from tray and presence of companion. | AND (to G2) | hospital database | 1 | The robot must retrieve this information before deciding the delivery method. |
| **AT2: Navigate to Room (Delivery)** | Navigate from kitchen to the inpatient’s room. | AND (to G4) | hospital corridor | 1 | Physical movement is required to reach the room. |
| **AT3: Open Door with Robot** | Open the room door using robot’s manipulation skill. | OR (to G7) | room door | 1 | Robot can open the door itself if it has the necessary skill. |
| **AT4: Place Food on Table** | Place the meal on the inpatient’s room table. | AND (to G4) | room table | 1 | The robot must physically place the food. |
| **AT5: Confirm Delivery** | Confirm that the meal has been placed on the table. | AND (to G4) | room table | 1 | Verification ensures the goal is satisfied. |
| **AT6: Navigate to Room (Fetch)** | Navigate from kitchen to the inpatient’s room for fetch. | AND (to G5) | hospital corridor | 1 | The robot must reach the room before it can hand over the tray. |
| **AT7: Open Door with Robot (Fetch)** | Open the room door using robot’s manipulation skill. | OR (to G7) | room door | 1 | Same as AT3; reused for fetch scenario. |
| **AT8: Ask Patient to Retrieve Meal** | Ask the patient (or companion) to retrieve the meal from the robot’s tray. | AND (to G5) | room | 1 | The robot must instruct the human to take the meal. |
| **AT9: Track Meal Retrieval** | Track when and where each meal was retrieved. | AND (to G5) | room | 1 | Logging is required for accountability and error detection. |
| **AT10: Alert Wrong Meal** | Alert if the wrong meal is retrieved. | AND (to G5) | room | 1 | The robot must monitor the retrieval and raise an alarm if a mismatch occurs. |
| **AT11: Confirm Retrieval** | Confirm that the meal has been retrieved by the patient. | AND (to G5) | room | 1 | Final confirmation that the meal is no longer in the robot’s possession. |
| **AT13: Open Door with Human** | Ask a human (companion, nurse, or other) to open the room door. | OR (to G7) | room door | 1 (robot initiates request) | Human assistance may be required if the robot cannot open the door itself. |
| **AT15: Pick Up Dishes Unassisted** | Pick up dirty dishes from the room without assistance. | OR (to G8) | room | 1 | The robot can lift dishes alone if they are light enough. |
| **AT16: Pick Up Dishes with Robot Cooperation** | Pick up dirty dishes from the room with cooperation of another robot. | OR (to G8) | room | 2 | Two robots can share the load for heavier dishes. |
| **AT17: Pick Up Dishes with Human Cooperation** | Pick up dirty dishes from the room with cooperation of a human. | OR (to G8) | room | 1 | Human help may be needed for bulky or heavy dishes. |

